(2436968, 333836, 16402, '<td valign="top">Sorry, DNMC.<br/> <br/>Main Entry: still life<br/>Function: noun<br/>Inflected Form(s): plural still lifes<br/>1 : a picture consisting predominantly of <i><b>inanimate</b></i> objects<br/>2 : the category of graphic arts concerned with <i><b>inanimate</b></i> subject matter</td>', 'Sorry, DNMC. Main Entry: still lifeFunction: nounInflected Form(s): plural still lifes1 : a picture consisting predominantly of inanimate objects2 : the category of graphic arts concerned with inanimate subject matter', '2006-05-19 17:05:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(2436979, 335600, 16402, '<td valign="top">Simplistic! Clean! Beautiful! One of the best of the challenge.</td>', 'Simplistic! Clean! Beautiful! One of the best of the challenge.', '2006-05-19 17:08:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(2437078, 333058, 34192, '<td valign="top">This is actually very good - technically and compositionally.  The only weak thing I can find is the lack of fill light on the right hand side, very slight blow out at the top.  The colors are forcing me to use the word marvelous.  Depth of field is excellent.  Okay, I just pulled the image into photoshop.  I''m wondering if your monitor displays darker than mine as I can see the line separating the wall and the ground.  If you darkened levels very slightly so that disappears and run a slight curves adjustment, the parts of the still life really pop.  Only added that as an insight - some people with dark or light monitors see differently.  Anyway, I think, for a boring subject (most all still lifes are boring), you creating an exceptional image that I could see in a garden magazine.  I like the lighting but feel a slight amount of fill on the right would help. If I was voting on this challenge, I would probably give this at least a 7 if not more.</td>', 'This is actually very good - technically and compositionally.  The only weak thing I can find is the lack of fill light on the right hand side, very slight blow out at the top.  The colors are forcing me to use the word marvelous.  Depth of field is excellent.  Okay, I just pulled the image into photoshop.  I''m wondering if your monitor displays darker than mine as I can see the line separating the wall and the ground.  If you darkened levels very slightly so that disappears and run a slight curves adjustment, the parts of the still life really pop.  Only added that as an insight - some people with dark or light monitors see differently.  Anyway, I think, for a boring subject (most all still lifes are boring), you creating an exceptional image that I could see in a garden magazine.  I like the lighting but feel a slight amount of fill on the right would help. If I was voting on this challenge, I would probably give this at least a 7 if not more.', '2006-05-19 17:29:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(2437096, 335258, 16402, '<td valign="top">Tighter crop at top would have improved this. Negative space really doesn''t add anything IMHO, but I really like it.</td>', 'Tighter crop at top would have improved this. Negative space really doesn''t add anything IMHO, but I really like it.', '2006-05-19 17:33:33.000000', NULL, 1),
