(2438013, 335442, 55746, '<td valign="top">Nicely done.  I would have prefered to have the glass of the watch to the back of the photo as the blur of it in the foreground is a bit distracting.  However, this photo is interesting and well lit.  Good job.</td>', 'Nicely done.  I would have prefered to have the glass of the watch to the back of the photo as the blur of it in the foreground is a bit distracting.  However, this photo is interesting and well lit.  Good job.', '2006-05-19 21:36:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(2438036, 335395, 34192, '<td valign="top">First, let me say that I do a lot of flower shots.  I know what goes into them and I know the thinking behind them.  That said, if I were voting on this in a basic challenge, I would give it a 7 (6 in advanced).  White flowers are extremely difficult as they essentially come with blown highlights.  :) Because of that, you really have to watch your lighting and not over-light the scene.  I like the overall texture here but I would like to see a little more texture in each individual petal.  I am not a fan of that shade of purple.  Personal preference.  Also, having the background match takes a little away touch of purple in the center.  But, I could think that just because I don''t like that color.  The composition is good.  I am back and forth on the depth of field used.  I like what you have and at the same time I like to see it deeper.  Overall, a good photo.  Just needs a little oomph from lightly more dramatic (less bright) lighting. To score an 8, fix the background color - black or white works for me. :) To score a 9, give me more raking light or back light - somethign with a little more drama.  I think Tuckersmom and Sher9204 have some of the more beautiful images of flowers that transcend the genre.</td>', 'First, let me say that I do a lot of flower shots.  I know what goes into them and I know the thinking behind them.  That said, if I were voting on this in a basic challenge, I would give it a 7 (6 in advanced).  White flowers are extremely difficult as they essentially come with blown highlights.  :) Because of that, you really have to watch your lighting and not over-light the scene.  I like the overall texture here but I would like to see a little more texture in each individual petal.  I am not a fan of that shade of purple.  Personal preference.  Also, having the background match takes a little away touch of purple in the center.  But, I could think that just because I don''t like that color.  The composition is good.  I am back and forth on the depth of field used.  I like what you have and at the same time I like to see it deeper.  Overall, a good photo.  Just needs a little oomph from lightly more dramatic (less bright) lighting. To score an 8, fix the background color - black or white works for me. :) To score a 9, give me more raking light or back light - somethign with a little more drama.  I think Tuckersmom and Sher9204 have some of the more beautiful images of flowers that transcend the genre.', '2006-05-19 21:46:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(2438086, 333749, 55746, '<td valign="top">Interesting subject.  There is a spot in the upper right hand corner that I find a bit distracting but I love the clarity of the pins so my eye tends to stay with the subject.  Nice lighting.  Well done.</td>', 'Interesting subject.  There is a spot in the upper right hand corner that I find a bit distracting but I love the clarity of the pins so my eye tends to stay with the subject.  Nice lighting.  Well done.', '2006-05-19 22:04:19.000000', NULL, 1),
