(2452685, 332787, 40465, '<td valign="top">Hi from Cpt2<br/> <br/>I liked this I gave it a 7.<br/> <br/>I like the bottles (my dad collects old medicine bottles.  the splash of red makes it an interesting photo.  It would have been dull otherwise, I think.<br/>The comp is ghood it leads one to the red pepper. The flowers are very pretty:)<br/> <br/>nicely done and well done on your top 3!!</td>', 'Hi from Cpt2 I liked this I gave it a 7. I like the bottles (my dad collects old medicine bottles.  the splash of red makes it an interesting photo.  It would have been dull otherwise, I think.The comp is ghood it leads one to the red pepper. The flowers are very pretty:) nicely done and well done on your top 3!!', '2006-05-24 11:15:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(2452725, 334513, 38496, '<td valign="top">Hi from CTP2:<br/> <br/>Way to go on the 4th place finish!!<br/> <br/>This is a nice clean shot, with a very elegant look to it.  The color tone is great, as is the lighting.  I kind of like the way my eye keeps jumping to the background and then coming back to the glass.  I''m having a hard time thinking of improvements.<br/>Great job!</td>', 'Hi from CTP2: Way to go on the 4th place finish!! This is a nice clean shot, with a very elegant look to it.  The color tone is great, as is the lighting.  I kind of like the way my eye keeps jumping to the background and then coming back to the glass.  I''m having a hard time thinking of improvements.Great job!', '2006-05-24 11:32:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2452734, 335258, 29011, '<td valign="top">You made the top10! congratulations. But agree with hotpasta, this should''ve ribboned :) but the company in the top10 sure is good.</td>', 'You made the top10! congratulations. But agree with hotpasta, this should''ve ribboned :) but the company in the top10 sure is good.', '2006-05-24 11:36:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(2452761, 335258, 24111, '<td valign="top">I love it!</td>', 'I love it!', '2006-05-24 11:53:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(2452763, 335151, 1570, '<td valign="top">thanks a lot for all your comments...</td>', 'thanks a lot for all your comments...', '2006-05-24 11:54:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(2452822, 334814, 43565, '<td valign="top">Actually, the definition for still life that I used was "a group of objects <b>artfully</b> arranged with lighting used to set a mood."   This, for me, is missing on the artful part.  Bathroom photos ususally get lower scores from me.</td>', 'Actually, the definition for still life that I used was "a group of objects artfully arranged with lighting used to set a mood."   This, for me, is missing on the artful part.  Bathroom photos ususally get lower scores from me.', '2006-05-24 12:18:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(2452838, 334818, 59065, '<td valign="top">Top 3 favorite for me, I''m really surprised it''s at 11.  I''m a sucker for B&amp;W though.  I think that is a french press in the back?  I would have filled it full of coffee, the condensation looks a little out of place.  Great shapes and arrangement.</td>', 'Top 3 favorite for me, I''m really surprised it''s at 11.  I''m a sucker for B&W though.  I think that is a french press in the back?  I would have filled it full of coffee, the condensation looks a little out of place.  Great shapes and arrangement.', '2006-05-24 12:24:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(2452839, 334814, 70, '<td valign="top">Okay, now that I''m done being a dink in the forums, I''ll leave you a comment. I didn''t vote in this challenge but if I had, I probably would have given you a 4. A few things..<br/> <br/>1. You''re right, the challenge title didn''t say "classic" anywhere in it. However, the challenge description says "This is a classic subject for many forms of art. Be creative and have fun!" Whenever you''re going to compete against 300+ other people, especially with backgrounds as varying as DPC voters, you really need to choose the moderate view of a challenge topic. That''s not to say that you can''t be creative within that topic, but you really do need to hit it dead on. Technically, your shot is of two inanimate things but they don''t fit the definition of a "typical" still life. Not only that but they are posed in an action scene which seems to contradict the idea of still life. <br/> <br/>2. The lighting is harsh and not in a way that''s complements the shot. The glare in her hair is especially hard on the eyes and the whole shot gives off a feeling of being under a giant spotlight, which isn''t typically where you are when you''re riding the porcelain bus. (You hope!)<br/> <br/>3. To borrow a few lines from Scalvert, "Toys usually fail because they scream "amateur." Look at past entries that scored in the 3.5-4.5 range and you''ll find them filled with whatever objects the photographer found handy around the house. Voters recognize a lack of effort and the punishment is severe." I wouldn''t necessarily say there was a lack of effort here but it''s still pretty difficult to score well with toys.<br/> <br/>4. The title is somewhat weak, has a typo and ends in an emoticon which denotes a lack of care and seriousness. If you want others to care about your work, take time to proofread and spellcheck your titles. <br/> <br/>Now then, these are just my opinions. I suspect a few other voters shared them but who can know for sure? Hopefully this helps a little.</td>', 'Okay, now that I''m done being a dink in the forums, I''ll leave you a comment. I didn''t vote in this challenge but if I had, I probably would have given you a 4. A few things.. 1. You''re right, the challenge title didn''t say "classic" anywhere in it. However, the challenge description says "This is a classic subject for many forms of art. Be creative and have fun!" Whenever you''re going to compete against 300+ other people, especially with backgrounds as varying as DPC voters, you really need to choose the moderate view of a challenge topic. That''s not to say that you can''t be creative within that topic, but you really do need to hit it dead on. Technically, your shot is of two inanimate things but they don''t fit the definition of a "typical" still life. Not only that but they are posed in an action scene which seems to contradict the idea of still life.  2. The lighting is harsh and not in a way that''s complements the shot. The glare in her hair is especially hard on the eyes and the whole shot gives off a feeling of being under a giant spotlight, which isn''t typically where you are when you''re riding the porcelain bus. (You hope!) 3. To borrow a few lines from Scalvert, "Toys usually fail because they scream "amateur." Look at past entries that scored in the 3.5-4.5 range and you''ll find them filled with whatever objects the photographer found handy around the house. Voters recognize a lack of effort and the punishment is severe." I wouldn''t necessarily say there was a lack of effort here but it''s still pretty difficult to score well with toys. 4. The title is somewhat weak, has a typo and ends in an emoticon which denotes a lack of care and seriousness. If you want others to care about your work, take time to proofread and spellcheck your titles.  Now then, these are just my opinions. I suspect a few other voters shared them but who can know for sure? Hopefully this helps a little.', '2006-05-24 12:25:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(2452840, 334785, 30222, '<td valign="top">regarding the challenge obviously lots of dnmc opinions<br/>i think here the discussion is not about the -inanimate thingie but if people were able and willing to see that composing the image is a pure form of -arranging especially when so conscious every element in the pic as i felt i did here, it would have helped i guess<br/>whatever<br/>its no surprise i dont attract large crowds<br/>better enjoy it underground while i can~)<br/>also its good to know people can get completely on the same wavelength every now and than))<br/>this site is about having fun isnt it<br/>a little simplification maybe;) but hey thats what im heading for !<br/></td>', 'regarding the challenge obviously lots of dnmc opinionsi think here the discussion is not about the -inanimate thingie but if people were able and willing to see that composing the image is a pure form of -arranging especially when so conscious every element in the pic as i felt i did here, it would have helped i guesswhateverits no surprise i dont attract large crowdsbetter enjoy it underground while i can~)also its good to know people can get completely on the same wavelength every now and than))this site is about having fun isnt ita little simplification maybe;) but hey thats what im heading for !', '2006-05-24 12:25:44.000000', NULL, 0),
