(2601689, 332774, 14986, '<td valign="top">I like this one but there are some things I would do if it was my shot.  I would have centered the plant shape (without the attachments) in front of the blinds and just simplified it by having the focus of the photo on the sillouette of the flower and the green light and shapes of the vase and the blinds.  I would have cropped so that you wouldn''t get any of the verticle seams/ropes part of the blinds.  You should restoot this one because I think it could be a really really cool almost abstract looking photo.</td>', 'I like this one but there are some things I would do if it was my shot.  I would have centered the plant shape (without the attachments) in front of the blinds and just simplified it by having the focus of the photo on the sillouette of the flower and the green light and shapes of the vase and the blinds.  I would have cropped so that you wouldn''t get any of the verticle seams/ropes part of the blinds.  You should restoot this one because I think it could be a really really cool almost abstract looking photo.', '2006-07-08 22:09:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(2623089, 335229, 37779, '<td valign="top">Wowza, those colors are hot and great! I''d have cropped the bottom a bit though. (But that''s just my preference)</td>', 'Wowza, those colors are hot and great! I''d have cropped the bottom a bit though. (But that''s just my preference)', '2006-07-14 19:26:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(2654466, 334168, 60003, '<td valign="top">I was reading the Zen thread and saw this picture in the very first post; it is an amazing and perfect example of Zen photography. This picture is so calming and naturally beautiful. I''m very new to photography, so I hope you don''t mind me asking, but how was the absolute clear white background without shadows achieved here? Again, lovely photograph.</td>', 'I was reading the Zen thread and saw this picture in the very first post; it is an amazing and perfect example of Zen photography. This picture is so calming and naturally beautiful. I''m very new to photography, so I hope you don''t mind me asking, but how was the absolute clear white background without shadows achieved here? Again, lovely photograph.', '2006-07-24 10:44:08.000000', NULL, 0),
